Conclusion
Key Findings:

Tesla's Growth Trajectory:

Stock price surged from $1.59 (2010) to over $900 (2021 peak), correlating with:

Expansion into mass-market vehicles (Model 3/Y)

Consistent revenue growth from $31M (Q3 2010) to $25B+ (2023)

Recent price corrections reflect market adjustments but maintain long-term upward trend

GameStop's Volatility:

Historic 2021 short squeeze ($20 to $483 in 3 months) despite:

Declining revenue from $9B+ (2018) to $5B (2023)

Fundamental business challenges from digital distribution

Demonstrates disconnect between stock performance and company fundamentals

Data Limitations:

Revenue figures lack explicit units (assumed millions/billions)

Web scraping fragility (website structure changes could break code)

Limited fundamental analysis (PE ratios, debt, etc.)
